 ## Conclusion
 
 In this workflow, we demonstrated how to perform a standard analysis pipeline on a subset of Visium HD data binned at 16 µm. Most methods and visualization techniques developed for Visium can be applied to Visium HD. However, more sparsity is expected, as each data point (e.g. 2, 8, or 16 µm) has smaller area compared to Visium (55 µm). Each bin cannot be interpreted as a cell, but rather, a segmentation-free approach is applied here. Below are some resources and news for Visium HD to consider and incorporate into your pipeline:
 
--   10x Genomics [news](https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/10x-genomics-unveils-innovation-roadmap-at-agbt-general-meeting-advancing-leadership-in-large-scale-single-cell-and-spatial-analysis-302382827.html) on morphology-driven segmentation from H&E enabled in CytAssist for Visium HD, by assigning transcripts to individual cells. 
-    - Space Ranger v4 now provides a segmented, cell-level count matrix under `segmented_outputs`, in parallel with the previous `binned_outputs` at 2, 8, and 16 µm, simplifying additional cell segmentation using `bin2cell` or `StarDist`. However, a comparative study of segmentation methods on Visium HD data has yet to be conducted. 
+- 10x Genomics [news](https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/10x-genomics-unveils-innovation-roadmap-at-agbt-general-meeting-advancing-leadership-in-large-scale-single-cell-and-spatial-analysis-302382827.html) on morphology-driven segmentation from H&E enabled in CytAssist for Visium HD, by assigning transcripts to individual cells. Notably, Space Ranger v4 provides a segmented, cell-level count matrix under `segmented_outputs`, in addition to the previous `binned_outputs` at 2, 8, and 16 µm, simplifying additional cell segmentation using `bin2cell` or `StarDist`. However, a comparative study of segmentation methods on Visium HD data has yet to be conducted. 
 
--   [GitHub repository of `bin2cell`](https://github.com/Teichlab/bin2cell) for H&E segmentation and obtaining cell boundaries.
+- [GitHub repository of `bin2cell`](https://github.com/Teichlab/bin2cell) for H&E segmentation and obtaining cell boundaries.
 
--   [Analysis pipeline](https://www.10xgenomics.com/analysis-guides/segmentation-visium-hd) by 10x Genomics (April 2024). The analysis consists of three steps: run `StarDist` nuclei segmentation in Python, sum gene expression into nuclei based on segmentation mask, and downstream analysis with `scanpy` and `anndata`.
